# ------------------------------------------------------------------ 7 listening 8-9
_L8A = [("Question", "Kung ikaw magpapamiyembro ka ng Philhealth kaagad-agad makukuha mo ang benefits o kailan po ’yan, dok?", "If you become a Philhealth member, will you get the benefits right away, or when is it, doc?"), ("Answer", "Ang general rule natin sa paggamit ng benefits dapat meron kang tatlong buwang hulog sa loob ng anim na buwan bago ang unang araw ng pagkakaospital. So halimbawa po ngayon, January, February, March. Kung bayad ka ng January, February, March by April puwede mo na siyang magamit.", "Our general rule for using the benefits is that you must have three months of contributions within six months before the first day of hospitalization. So for example now, January, February, March. If you have paid January, February, March, by April you can already use it.")]
_L8B = [("Question", "Sir, matanong ko lamang po para maging maliwanag sa ating mga kababayang OFWs kapag nasa ibang bansa sila habang nagtatrabaho doon sila inabutan ng pagkakasakit ano. Paano po ’yung proseso nito para magamit nila ang Philhealth?", "Sir, I would just like to ask, to make it clear for our countrymen who are OFWs, when they are abroad working and illness catches them there, what is the process for them to use Philhealth?"), ("Answer", "Well, para po sa ating mga OFW or hindi man, kahit tayo. Alam n’yo naman ang mga Pilipino ngayon, mahilig mag-travel. Uhm, pag tayo po ang inabutan ng pagkakasakit sa ibang bansa magagamit pa rin natin ang Philhealth. Yun nga lang hindi po siya yung automatic deduction diyan sa mga hospital. Ano po ang gagawin? So, tayo muna ang magbabayad ng ating billing. Tapos po, kailangan nating magsubmit sa Philhealth ng ating medical certificate kung saan nakapaloob doon kung ano ang pagkakasakit, saan na-confine, ilang araw, at ibibigay din po natin ang official receipt ng pinagbayadan.", "Well, for our OFWs, or not, even for us. You know that Filipinos nowadays love to travel. Um, if illness catches us in another country we can still use Philhealth. It is just that there is no automatic deduction at the hospitals there. What do we do? So we pay our billing first. Then we need to submit to Philhealth our medical certificate, which states what the illness is, where we were confined, how many days, and we also give the official receipt of what we paid.")]
_L8C = [("Question", "What are the process kung paano makapag-register?", "What is the process for how to register?"), ("Answer", "Actually, napakadali lang especially sa ating mga senior citizens. Ang kinakailangan lang po ninyo, magpunta po kayo sa tinatawag nating Office of Senior Citizen’s Affairs o OSCA sa inyong mga lugar. At doon po magpi-fill up po kayo ng ating Member’s Registration Form. Ang OSCA na po ang bahalang magpadala sa Philhealth nitong mga papel na ’to. At pagka kayo’y miyembro, ipapa-register na at pagbalik po bibigyan na nila kayo ng tinatawag na member data record. Napakadali lang. Actually even ang member, kasi ang mga senior citizens maaring may sakit na and some of them probably baka nahihirapan nang maglakad. So hindi naman nangangailangan na sila po ang mismong pupunta, puwede namang authorized representative. Puwede rin po ’yun.", "Actually, it is very easy, especially for our senior citizens. All you need to do is go to what we call the Office of Senior Citizen’s Affairs (OSCA) in your area. And there you will fill up our Member’s Registration Form. OSCA will be the one to send these papers to Philhealth. And once you are a member, you will be registered and on returning they will give you what is called a member data record. It is very easy. Actually, even the member, since senior citizens may already be sick and some of them probably have difficulty walking, they do not need to be the ones to come themselves, an authorized representative can do it. That is also fine.")]
_K8 = [("Passage 1, item 1: main idea", "The date of effectivity of Philhealth benefits."), ("Passage 1, item 2: the general rule (2 details)", "The general rule is that you must have 3 months of contributions within a 6-month period before your first day of hospitalization. For example, if you pay your contributions during the months of January, February, and March, you can use the benefits in April."), ("Passage 2, item 3: what the question was about", "In case an OFW gets sick overseas, what is the process or procedure so he or she could avail of Philhealth benefits?"), ("Passage 2, item 4: three steps or requisites", "She or he should first pay the medical bills. Then submit to Philhealth a medical certificate indicating the type of illness, place and duration of confinement. She or he should also submit official receipts as proof of payments."), ("Passage 3, item 5: main idea", "How senior citizens should register for Philhealth membership; the registration process of senior citizens to become Philhealth members."), ("Passage 3, item 6: the steps", "First, the senior citizen should go to the local office of the Office of Senior Citizen’s Affairs (OSCA). Fill up the Member’s Registration Form (MRF). OSCA will send the form to the Philhealth office. Once a member, you will be registered, then Philhealth will issue a member data record. If a senior citizen is unable to go due to illness, she or he could send an authorized representative.")]
_L9 = [("Narrator", "Noong Hunyo ng taong dalawang libo at labintatlo nagkaroon tayo ng bagong batas, tinatawag na R.A. sampung libo, anim na raan at anim. Ano po yung nandodoon. Unang-una pinadali na po ng batas ang pagpapamiyembro sa Philhealth. Wala na tayong kailangang requirements. So ang kailangan na lang po natin, i-fill up natin ang PMRF o yung Philhealth Member Registration Form, isulat lang yun, kumpletuhin ang impormasyon, i-file sa Philhealth, bibigyan ng numero ng Philhealth, puwede na tayong magbayad. Wala na pong kailangang requirements. So, yung mga birth certificate, marriage contract hindi na natin siya hinihingi ngayon.", "In June 2013 we had a new law, called R.A. 10606. What is in it? First of all, the law has made becoming a PhilHealth member easier. We no longer need requirements. So all we need is to fill up the PMRF, or the Philhealth Member Registration Form, just write it, complete the information, file it with Philhealth, we are given a Philhealth number, and we can pay. There are no more requirements. So the birth certificate and marriage contract we no longer ask for now.")]
_K9 = [("1. An important provision of R.A. 10606", "R.A. 10606 provides for expedited application for membership to Philhealth."), ("2. The requirements under R.A. 10606 (3 details)", "There are no requirements. The applicant only needs to fill up the PMRF, or Philhealth Member Registration Form, complete the information, then submit the form. Philhealth will give the applicant a Philhealth number, then the applicant proceeds to pay the monthly contribution. Marriage contract and birth certificate are no longer required.")]
